# CodeEraser binary distribution manifest (ADR-007: SHA256 pinned in
# the plugin manifest). Sourced by bin/ce.sh — plain sh key=value so
# the starter needs no JSON parser. The release flow is two-phase
# (build->pin->tag, docs/RELEASE.md):
# a workflow_dispatch run uploads draft artifacts + SHA256SUMS, the
# measured hashes land HERE in a commit, and only then the tag is cut,
# whose workflow verifies the draft assets against these pins before
# publishing. Empty pins = air-gapped preview stance: ce.sh falls back
# to a manually placed binary or `ce` on PATH and never downloads.

CE_MANIFEST_VERSION="1.8.0"
CE_BASE_URL="https://github.com/skymanbp/CodeEraser/releases/download/v1.8.0"

# Per-platform pins, filled by the release pin commit. Key grammar:
# CE_SHA256_<PLATFORM>_CE where <PLATFORM> is the uname-derived key
# with [a-z-] uppercased to [A-Z_] (see plat_key in ce.sh). The roster
# is update::version::TARGETS — five targets since v1.7.0 (plan v2.29
# step 10, O70); the two newer keys stay EMPTY until the first release
# that builds them is pinned, the air-gapped stance above meanwhile.
CE_SHA256_X86_64_WINDOWS_CE="76c202a9a1e6170d03a74df12156b47949e05f82b796c7e1d7e6edd90e6f02fb"
CE_SHA256_X86_64_LINUX_CE="241399b5d3a8db3704822e9f6c9378e718a09c05410be225a8cee499e1744c2f"
CE_SHA256_AARCH64_MACOS_CE="c5383f746af9119fe4ab5241f06641ce945b5ac65f0d645434eabea898332aae"
CE_SHA256_X86_64_MACOS_CE="1f302a41c2f98acffad9399a33b632db7d9d984fd261202259417057012e3232"
CE_SHA256_AARCH64_LINUX_CE="d92bef206f99211e501bce334ff2c81d5992a50647650728c8a974f1b1bc0447"

# ce-core (the Haskell judgment layer) ships beside ce from v0.2.0 —
# ce.sh places it as a plain `ce-core` sibling in CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA,
# which is exactly where ce's resolver chain probes. Empty pins =
# the core download leg stays off (judgment families then need a
# source-installed ce-core, the pre-v0.2.0 stance).
CE_SHA256_X86_64_WINDOWS_CECORE="a48b8750a92a00fa56af259ce90bf3cf82f15267f18333a27e6c95e9af9aec1c"
CE_SHA256_X86_64_LINUX_CECORE="6e7571d6f9db5c1955d0df427997b5ef7f1ba593e09f3d7da5b7ff7bb1f404fe"
CE_SHA256_AARCH64_MACOS_CECORE="bd0da675c026939bdc9bf82119a12e35eb09b09c65623c45f0408695b2c764d4"
CE_SHA256_X86_64_MACOS_CECORE="3f24cb532630ce4cbe5a873ee997285c22b09d16548956d6c64914fb9ba972a3"
CE_SHA256_AARCH64_LINUX_CECORE="2bfb7bd96828a4d490febb26a24106da2f55eec0abf129de75fb4b07e81d42f0"

# The GUI installers, one per target (pinned since v0.7.3 — acf2095,
# the commit that first committed them; the version these pins
# measure is CE_MANIFEST_VERSION above — no second copy of it here
# to rot): the highest-privilege artifacts in the release — elevated,
# and the Windows one edits the machine PATH — were the only assets
# with no committed pin, checked solely against a SHA256SUMS
# generated by the same mutable draft. The tag phase verifies these
# too, so the trust anchor covers every binary the release ships.
CE_SHA256_X86_64_WINDOWS_SETUP="a4b66f950a4ac00cfdf4373f6c27211dcc7796012e9b624cf7fb7c6235a4614d"
CE_SHA256_X86_64_LINUX_APPIMAGE="a836cba42703b8197c815908e70f0ef7b1cb09b1f787725906b7a7e1a976fd6d"
CE_SHA256_AARCH64_MACOS_DMG="b0db4d8b6d3a4b7c9a11b03d43ac5bc5fc9ead9065239a8d9c4479089e4486a9"
CE_SHA256_X86_64_MACOS_DMG="0ad2945a7326939fa6300e759d8d8d794435fcfaeb7e8f39499948ba5acd03e7"
CE_SHA256_AARCH64_LINUX_APPIMAGE="a13de07a3dff8c78e1d865b52e93f0d416e1eb357664060578261c63119fa346"
